  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nUpper trough over the western states has been weakening allowing\nthe rainshowers over the eastern zones to move off to the\nnortheast of the CWA. Temperatures are again cooler than normal\nwith expected highs in the mid 60s to low 70s, about 10 to 15\ndegrees below normal.\n\nModels are progging that the upper ridge to our southeast will\nrebound a bit this weekend. But with the abundant low-level\nmoisture around, any of the sun's energy will initially go into\nevaporation. Thus highs on Saturday will once again be below\nnormal. Also, fog doesn/t look to be a major concern for Saturday\nmorning as abundant clouds tonight should keep radiational cooling\nfrom occurring. Later shifts may have more info on this, so some\npatchy fog is possible come Saturday morning.\n\nAdditional warming is expected Sunday with more sunshine. Look for\nhighs in the mid 70s to low 80s with light winds. Similar\nconditions are expected Monday. Clouds will increase late in the\nday with the next disturbance moving in.\n\nModels then have showers and cooler conditions for Tuesday that\nlinger into Wednesday. Rainfall amounts should be less than a \nquarter inch in a 24 hour period. Could be enough to cause travel\nissues for unpaved roadways but also keep the fire danger low.\n\nSaid disturbance moves out Wednesday with a return to warmer and\ndrier conditions for the end of the week.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nOverall, NBM held the line through much of the forecast period.\nConfidence is increasing on mainly dry conditions this weekend\nwith a warmup through Monday. TFJ",
